In article <19822@cbmvax.commodore.com> daveb@cbmvax.commodore.com (Dave Berezowski) writes:
>	Has anyone gotten 'Amiga NetHack 3.0 PL10' to save a game when run
>by double-clicking on the 'NetHack' icon?  I can only save a game if I run
>the program from the 'NewGame' icon.
You're not supposed to run from the NetHack icon - you should do a Duplicate
on the NewGame icon so you can customize the ToolTypes as you wish and play
from THAT icon (see the docs).
>  I did some snooping via 'SnoopDos'
>and discovered that NetHack is trying to open a file called 'G:NetHack'
I'll look into this.
>I have my nethack.cnf file
>set to 'SAVE=NetHack:save' but the 'save' dir is never referenced.
This is where games are saved when you play from the command line.  When you
play from WorkBench, the game is saved wherever the icon lives.
